```console
$ um run list --help
List Useful Machinery runs

Usage: um run list [OPTIONS] <ORGANIZATION>

Arguments:
  <ORGANIZATION>  Organization ID or exact slug

Options:
      --project-id <PROJECT>
          Project ID
      --state-group <STATE_GROUP>
          Filter by run state group [possible values: active, terminal]
      --created-after <RFC3339>
          List runs created strictly after this time
      --integration-context <KEY=VALUE>
          Match an exact integration context entry (repeatable)
      --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum runs to return (1-100)
      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Opaque continuation cursor
      --json
          Print the run result as JSON
      --service-api-key-file <PATH|->
          Authenticate with a service API key from a private file, or - for standard input
      --allow-insecure-http
          Allow this command's Useful Machinery requests over insecure HTTP connections
  -h, --help
          Print help

Pagination:
  This command returns one page. Pass --cursor <CURSOR> to continue.

```
